{
  "book": "Micah",
  "commentary": "Darby Translation Notes",
  "author": "John Nelson Darby",
  "entries": [
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 1,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 1,
      "title": "",
      "content": "(b-0) (The title of this Book, 'Micah'), Meaning, Who is like Jah? see ch. 7.18; Ps. 68.4."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 8,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 8,
      "title": "",
      "content": "stripped (a-13) Or 'barefooted.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 10,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 10,
      "title": "",
      "content": "all; (b-9) Or 'in Acco (i.e. 'weeping') weep not.' Vers. 10-15 are made up of paranomasia, see Isa. 5.7 Beth-le-aphrah (c-11) House of dust."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 11,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 11,
      "title": "",
      "content": "Shaphir, (d-5) Beautiful town. Zaanan (e-13) Coming forth, Josh. 15.37. Beth-ezel. (f-22) Neighbouring house. will (g-24) Or '... forth; the lamentation of Beth-ezel will.' shelter. (h-29) Or 'stay.' lit. 'standing [ground].'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 12,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 12,
      "title": "",
      "content": "Maroth (i-5) Bitterness."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 14,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 14,
      "title": "",
      "content": "Moresheth-Gath. (k-7) Possession of Gath. Achzib (l-11) Lying."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 15,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 15,
      "title": "",
      "content": "heir, (m-8) Or, 'the possessor.' Mareshah; (n-12) Possession, inheritance. Adullam. (o-21) Or 'Even unto Adullam (meaning 'retreat') shall he come, -- the glory of Israel.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 1,
      "start_verse": 16,
      "end_chapter": 1,
      "end_verse": 16,
      "title": "",
      "content": "eagle, (p-18) Or 'vulture.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 2,
      "start_verse": 1,
      "end_chapter": 2,
      "end_verse": 1,
      "title": "",
      "content": "work (q-8) See Note m, Ps. 5.5. hand. (r-29) Or 'because for them their hand is God (El).' see Prov. 3.27."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 2,
      "start_verse": 2,
      "end_chapter": 2,
      "end_verse": 2,
      "title": "",
      "content": "oppress (s-18) Or 'defraud,' see Ezek. 22.12. man (t-20) Geber, Job 3.3. man (u-26) Ish, Gen. 2.23."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 2,
      "start_verse": 6,
      "end_chapter": 2,
      "end_verse": 6,
      "title": "",
      "content": "Prophesy (v-1) Lit. 'Drop,' in this and ver. 11, as Amos 7.16. these, (w-12) i.e. If the true prophets do not prophesy to the unjust rich men (see vers. 1,2). others translate 'They shall not prophesy of such.'"
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 2,
      "start_verse": 7,
      "end_chapter": 2,
      "end_verse": 7,
      "title": "",
      "content": "impatient? (x-12) Or 'Is the Spirit of Jehovah straitened?' to (y-23) Lit. 'with.' (z-0) This note set is not public domain."
    },
    {
      "start_chapter": 2,
      "start_verse": 8,
      "end_chapter": 2,
      "end_verse": 8,
      "title": "",
      "content": "with (a-17) Lit. 'from off.' averse (b-28) Or 'as coming back.'"
    },
